maria: quick sync — PR #842 just landed to migrate the structured-output docs to the new function/tool-calling guidance. needs: 1) updated SDK snippets (py/ts), 2) clearer JSON schema examples for optional array fields, 3) guardrail prose re: fallback parsing, 4) a couple broken links i found. pinging reviewers for quick triage :eyes:

sam: on it. which files are failing link checks? i saw one in `docs/reference/tool-calling.md` earlier.

maria: exact ones: 1) /docs/guides/parse-patterns -> redirect to /docs/guides/parsing-patterns (404), 2) old API anchor `/api#function-calling` -> should be `/api#tool-calling`. i left inline comments in the PR.

leo: i can take SDK snippets. want me to replace the old `call_function()` examples with the SDK's new `invoke_tool()` and show both sync + streaming?

anjali: yes please. also we should add a tiny example for graceful fallback when schema validation fails. recommend 2-paragraph pattern + tiny code block showing the heuristic: try JSON.parse -> validate against schema -> if fail, call `extract_from_text()` fallback.

patrick: tagging docs-ci-bot — is the schema lint action currently flaky? i ran `make docs-check` locally and it passed but CI timed out on examples lint step.

"docs-ci-bot": build triggered: docs/lint -> running snippet-checker and link-audit. results will post here in ~5m. (status updates below)

sam: for the JSON schema examples, please prefer `oneOf` with clear comments rather than nullable unions; we've seen downstream parsers choke on `type: ["object","null"]`. propose adding an example for array canonicalization: show both `[]` and `null` handling and a canonicalization snippet in JS.

maria: good call. add that snippet near the "Array / Null handling" section. also add a short note under "Guardrails" that callers should keep an off-ramp: if validation fails after N attempts, return `{"error":"unparseable"}` and surface to ops.

leo: here's a compact TS example i drafted for the PR that we can paste into docs (will push to the branch):
```ts
// canonicalize-array.ts
function canonicalizeArray(value: any): any[] {
  if (Array.isArray(value)) return value;
  if (value == null) return [];
  if (typeof value === 'string') {
    try { return JSON.parse(value); } catch { return [value]; }
  }
  return [value];
}
```

anjali: perfect. i'll add a 2-line explanation above it and a note that this is a heuristic: better to surface a clear schema to the model and use guardrails when possible.

patrick: docs-ci-bot update: snippet-checker passed, link-audit - found two broken links (the ones maria listed). docs build succeeded but examples-lint timed out on one matrix job. opening a follow-up job.

maria: ok volunteers: @leo for SDK snippets (TS + short Python), @anjali for guardrail wording + fallback example, @sam for link fixes and running final CI. i'll shepherd the merge once CI is green. target to merge today EOD.

sam: copying the exact file paths to fix in the PR comments so it's easy: `/docs/guides/parse-patterns.md` -> `/docs/guides/parsing-patterns.md`, and change anchor `#function-calling` -> `#tool-calling` in `/docs/reference/tool-calling.md`.

leo: i'll push snippet updates in the next 20m. python snippet will use `from redwood import client; client.invoke_tool(...)`. keep it compact.

anjali: added guardrail paragraph and fallback example in a small commit to the branch. left a TODO to add an eval fixture showing regression for the fallback pattern.

maria: amazing — thanks all. once CI is fully green i'll merge. if anything blocks, @maria please DM. :rocket:
